  -> Constants are used to store values that should not change throughout the program. 
   They provide a way to define fixed values that can be referenced multiple times without the risk of accidental reassignment.

General Convention
------------------

-> Use camelCase for regular const variables:

         const userName = "Nandhini";
         const totalPrice = 500;

-> Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for values that are true constants/configuration values:

        const PI = 3.14;
        const MAX_RETRIES = 3;
        const API_URL = "https://api.example.com";